{"id":101,"explanation":"Do not cache get_user results for the life of the process. If a user's role is revoked, a cached result could keep reporting the old role. #640 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"Check db.Query's error before deferring rows.Close(). When the query fails, rows is nil, so calling Close on it would be unsafe.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"The zero-delay setTimeout is a deliberate choice for scheduling measure(el): the layout needs to settle before the measurement runs. The comment says queueMicrotask should not replace it.","unsure":"“Layout must settle” does not specify which pending layout change the code is waiting for."}
{"id":104,"explanation":"The token has type Secret<String>. Never log its contents; if it is formatted with Debug, the output must contain only a redacted value.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"RetryCount is coupled to the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json. A developer changing either value must update the other to match. appsettings.json is the configuration file, and Http.Retry is the setting within it.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"Before mapping the buffer, ensure offset is divisible by pageSize with no remainder. The memory mapping operation rejects an offset that is not page aligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"In this rsync command, the trailing slash on build/ makes rsync copy the contents of build into $DEST, rather than copying the build directory itself. The comment flags this behavior of the external rsync command.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The BRIN index on events.created_at is chosen for size: the comment says it is about 1% the size of a btree index. That choice relies on events being appended in time order.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"The loop currently waits by spinning and should eventually be replaced with a futex based wait. The stated completion condition is that lock_acquire, the symbol in src/sync/lock.c, sleeps while waiting.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"The reason dbo.RebuildStats runs on the secondary is documented in the failover section of the runbook. doc:runbook#failover points to that document and anchor.","unsure":"The comment does not give the runbook's file path or the reason itself."}
{"id":111,"explanation":"The timeout of 30 seconds is kept below 60 seconds because an upstream proxy terminates requests that have been idle for 60 seconds. The comment describes a constraint imposed by that external proxy.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"Keep Widget's destructor virtual. If ~Widget() is made non-virtual, deleting a derived object through a Widget pointer could skip the derived destructor. #915 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"Enable SQLite foreign key enforcement on this connection before any write. The setting applies per connection, so enabling it elsewhere does not cover this connection.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"Name uses the fixed-capacity ShortString form string[40] deliberately because the record is written directly to disk byte for byte. Replacing it with string would change the record's stored representation.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"p_id is caller input, so the dynamic DELETE must pass it through the :1 bind variable, as the USING clause does. Concatenating that input into the EXECUTE IMMEDIATE SQL text could allow SQL injection.","unsure":""}
